ower speak truth to  power and then to fund local activists  who are actually on the ground doing the  work now something positive like this  will not happen without conservative  backlash and I want to read you a couple  of tweets from conservatives who lost  their minds the first one here on  Twitter says this first the NFL forces  me to choose between my favorite sport  and my country  I choose country then Nike forces me to  choose between my favorite shoes and my  country so when did the American flag  and the national anthem become offensive  now I wanted to read you that tweet from  someone who seems to be just a random  Twitter user because he shared video  with it take a look at this video here  I'm on joy hell I might buy go buy some  adidas hmm you know how many other  sneakers are to buy to choose from there  to go ahead you're gonna go ahead and  say hey buy him our shoes we stand with  people who kneel for the national anthem  well sorry Nike I've been buying you for  the past 20 plus years not anymore  not only am i burning my favorite pair  of Nikes you are burning your sails have  a good day I mean you know it's it's  ridiculous people make these scenes and  obviously their publicity stunts they  want attention and so they burn their  apparel they did this win when LeBron  James and up the Cleveland Cavaliers and  that trend never ended but the reality  of it is is that Nike doesn't care about  the handful of people they've already  made the calculation this is a business  decision for Nike they have already  calculated the cost how much they're  going to lose from conservatives who are  mad and how much when they make up in  terms of people who are like hmm Nikes  doing something good with all of the  products from their sweatshops so maybe  I'll go and buy some shoes and we'll  talk about that later but the point is  is that this is a business decision by  Nike and so they know full well exactly  about how many people they're gonna lose  they know